{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This walkthrough uses the framework-agnostic DOM host. The same chart\ndefinition passes unchanged to any supported\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./installation.md#framework-compatibility","children":[{"type":"text","value":"framework adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install TanStack Charts:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/charts","lang":"sh"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-add-a-chart-container","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Add a chart container"}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div id=\"monthly-revenue-chart\"></div>","lang":"html"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The host follows the container width when "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"width"},{"type":"text","value":" is omitted."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-define-the-data-and-chart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Define the data and chart"}]},{"type":"html","value":"<!-- docs-example: core-quick-start typecheck -->"},{"type":"code","value":"import { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { scalePoint } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/point'\nimport { defineChart, lineY, mountChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\ninterface RevenueMonth {\n  month: string\n  revenue: number\n}\n\nconst monthlyRevenue: readonly RevenueMonth[] = [\n  { month: 'Jan', revenue: 42_000 },\n  { month: 'Feb', revenue: 58_000 },\n  { month: 'Mar', revenue: 76_000 },\n  { month: 'Apr', revenue: 64_000 },\n  { month: 'May', revenue: 81_000 },\n]\n\nconst monthlyRevenueChart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    lineY(monthlyRevenue, {\n      id: 'monthly-revenue',\n      x: 'month',\n      y: 'revenue',\n      points: true,\n      stroke: '#2563eb',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: () => scalePoint<string>().padding(0.2),\n      axis: { label: 'Month' },\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: { label: 'Revenue (USD)' },\n    },\n  },\n\n  tooltip,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The compact point and linear scales cover this categorical and numeric chart\nwithout a D3 dependency. The original revenue row flows through the mark and\ninto interaction callbacks; no cast or manual chart generic is needed."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-mount-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Mount it"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const container = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#monthly-revenue-chart')\n\nif (!container) {\n  throw new Error('Missing #monthly-revenue-chart container')\n}\n\nconst options = {\n  definition: monthlyRevenueChart,\n  height: 360,\n  initialWidth: 640,\n  ariaLabel: 'Monthly revenue',\n}\n\nconst host = mountChart(container, options)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialWidth"},{"type":"text","value":" is the deterministic fallback for server output, hidden containers, and the first frame before measurement. Once visible, the host uses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ResizeObserver"},{"type":"text","value":" to follow the container."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-update-the-chart","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Update the chart"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Host options only cover mounting concerns such as size and accessibility:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"host.update({\n  ...options,\n  height: 420,\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When data, visual options, focus, tooltips, keyboard policy, or animation\nchange, create a new definition and pass it to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"host.update"},{"type":"text","value":". In a framework\ncomponent, memoize the complete definition against the values it captures. See\n"},{"type":"link","href":"./concepts/chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart definitions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"5-clean-up","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Clean up"}]},{"type":"code","value":"host.destroy()","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Destroying the host removes observers, event listeners, animations, tooltips, and chart markup. Framework adapters do this automatically during unmount."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-the-declaration-means","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the declaration means"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lineY(monthlyRevenue, ...)"},{"type":"text","value":" chooses a line mark and keeps each source row as\nthe interaction datum."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"x: 'month'"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"y: 'revenue'"},{"type":"text","value":" map existing source fields."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The unique month gives each observation stable positional identity across updates."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Compact scale factories infer domains from mark channels and own mapping behavior."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Charts copies those scales and assigns responsive pixel ranges."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"label"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"format"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"grid"},{"type":"text","value":" configure the axis guide without changing the scale."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Omitted margins are measured automatically from the rendered labels and titles."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ariaLabel"},{"type":"text","value":" names the chart; pointer and keyboard focus use the same inferred points."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read "},{"type":"link","href":"./concepts/grammar-of-graphics.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grammar of Graphics"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the full model, then browse the "},{"type":"link","href":"./examples/index.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example Gallery"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for complete compositions."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-add-a-chart-container","text":"1. Add a chart container","level":2},{"id":"2-define-the-data-and-chart","text":"2. Define the data and chart","level":2},{"id":"3-mount-it","text":"3. Mount it","level":2},{"id":"4-update-the-chart","text":"4. Update the chart","level":2},{"id":"5-clean-up","text":"5. Clean up","level":2},{"id":"what-the-declaration-means","text":"What the declaration means","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis walkthrough uses the framework-agnostic DOM host. The same chart\ndefinition passes unchanged to any supported\n[framework adapter](./installation.md#framework-compatibility).\n\nInstall TanStack Charts:\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts\n```\n\n## 1. Add a chart container\n\n```html\n<div id=\"monthly-revenue-chart\"></div>\n```\n\nThe host follows the container width when `width` is omitted.\n\n## 2. Define the data and chart\n\n<!-- docs-example: core-quick-start typecheck -->\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { scalePoint } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/point'\nimport { defineChart, lineY, mountChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\ninterface RevenueMonth {\n  month: string\n  revenue: number\n}\n\nconst monthlyRevenue: readonly RevenueMonth[] = [\n  { month: 'Jan', revenue: 42_000 },\n  { month: 'Feb', revenue: 58_000 },\n  { month: 'Mar', revenue: 76_000 },\n  { month: 'Apr', revenue: 64_000 },\n  { month: 'May', revenue: 81_000 },\n]\n\nconst monthlyRevenueChart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    lineY(monthlyRevenue, {\n      id: 'monthly-revenue',\n      x: 'month',\n      y: 'revenue',\n      points: true,\n      stroke: '#2563eb',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: () => scalePoint<string>().padding(0.2),\n      axis: { label: 'Month' },\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: { label: 'Revenue (USD)' },\n    },\n  },\n\n  tooltip,\n})\n```\n\nThe compact point and linear scales cover this categorical and numeric chart\nwithout a D3 dependency. The original revenue row flows through the mark and\ninto interaction callbacks; no cast or manual chart generic is needed.\n\n## 3. Mount it\n\n```ts\nconst container = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#monthly-revenue-chart')\n\nif (!container) {\n  throw new Error('Missing #monthly-revenue-chart container')\n}\n\nconst options = {\n  definition: monthlyRevenueChart,\n  height: 360,\n  initialWidth: 640,\n  ariaLabel: 'Monthly revenue',\n}\n\nconst host = mountChart(container, options)\n```\n\n`initialWidth` is the deterministic fallback for server output, hidden containers, and the first frame before measurement. Once visible, the host uses `ResizeObserver` to follow the container.\n\n## 4. Update the chart\n\nHost options only cover mounting concerns such as size and accessibility:\n\n```ts\nhost.update({\n  ...options,\n  height: 420,\n})\n```\n\nWhen data, visual options, focus, tooltips, keyboard policy, or animation\nchange, create a new definition and pass it to `host.update`. In a framework\ncomponent, memoize the complete definition against the values it captures. See\n[Chart definitions](./concepts/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## 5. Clean up\n\n```ts\nhost.destroy()\n```\n\nDestroying the host removes observers, event listeners, animations, tooltips, and chart markup. Framework adapters do this automatically during unmount.\n\n## What the declaration means\n\n- `lineY(monthlyRevenue, ...)` chooses a line mark and keeps each source row as\n  the interaction datum.\n- `x: 'month'` and `y: 'revenue'` map existing source fields.\n- The unique month gives each observation stable positional identity across updates.\n- Compact scale factories infer domains from mark channels and own mapping behavior.\n- TanStack Charts copies those scales and assigns responsive pixel ranges.\n- `label`, `format`, and `grid` configure the axis guide without changing the scale.\n- Omitted margins are measured automatically from the rendered labels and titles.\n- `ariaLabel` names the chart; pointer and keyboard focus use the same inferred points.\n\nRead [Grammar of Graphics](./concepts/grammar-of-graphics.md) for the full model, then browse the [Example Gallery](./examples/index.md) for complete compositions.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Quick Start\ndescription: Build, mount, update, and clean up a responsive TanStack Charts line chart with fully inferred types.\n---\n\nThis walkthrough uses the framework-agnostic DOM host. The same chart\ndefinition passes unchanged to any supported\n[framework adapter](./installation.md#framework-compatibility).\n\nInstall TanStack Charts:\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts\n```\n\n## 1. Add a chart container\n\n```html\n<div id=\"monthly-revenue-chart\"></div>\n```\n\nThe host follows the container width when `width` is omitted.\n\n## 2. Define the data and chart\n\n<!-- docs-example: core-quick-start typecheck -->\n\n```ts\nimport { scaleLinear } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/linear'\nimport { scalePoint } from '@tanstack/charts/scales/point'\nimport { defineChart, lineY, mountChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\ninterface RevenueMonth {\n  month: string\n  revenue: number\n}\n\nconst monthlyRevenue: readonly RevenueMonth[] = [\n  { month: 'Jan', revenue: 42_000 },\n  { month: 'Feb', revenue: 58_000 },\n  { month: 'Mar', revenue: 76_000 },\n  { month: 'Apr', revenue: 64_000 },\n  { month: 'May', revenue: 81_000 },\n]\n\nconst monthlyRevenueChart = defineChart({\n  marks: [\n    lineY(monthlyRevenue, {\n      id: 'monthly-revenue',\n      x: 'month',\n      y: 'revenue',\n      points: true,\n      stroke: '#2563eb',\n    }),\n  ],\n  scales: {\n    x: {\n      scale: () => scalePoint<string>().padding(0.2),\n      axis: { label: 'Month' },\n    },\n    y: {\n      scale: scaleLinear,\n      nice: true,\n      grid: true,\n      axis: { label: 'Revenue (USD)' },\n    },\n  },\n\n  tooltip,\n})\n```\n\nThe compact point and linear scales cover this categorical and numeric chart\nwithout a D3 dependency. The original revenue row flows through the mark and\ninto interaction callbacks; no cast or manual chart generic is needed.\n\n## 3. Mount it\n\n```ts\nconst container = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('#monthly-revenue-chart')\n\nif (!container) {\n  throw new Error('Missing #monthly-revenue-chart container')\n}\n\nconst options = {\n  definition: monthlyRevenueChart,\n  height: 360,\n  initialWidth: 640,\n  ariaLabel: 'Monthly revenue',\n}\n\nconst host = mountChart(container, options)\n```\n\n`initialWidth` is the deterministic fallback for server output, hidden containers, and the first frame before measurement. Once visible, the host uses `ResizeObserver` to follow the container.\n\n## 4. Update the chart\n\nHost options only cover mounting concerns such as size and accessibility:\n\n```ts\nhost.update({\n  ...options,\n  height: 420,\n})\n```\n\nWhen data, visual options, focus, tooltips, keyboard policy, or animation\nchange, create a new definition and pass it to `host.update`. In a framework\ncomponent, memoize the complete definition against the values it captures. See\n[Chart definitions](./concepts/chart-definitions.md).\n\n## 5. Clean up\n\n```ts\nhost.destroy()\n```\n\nDestroying the host removes observers, event listeners, animations, tooltips, and chart markup. Framework adapters do this automatically during unmount.\n\n## What the declaration means\n\n- `lineY(monthlyRevenue, ...)` chooses a line mark and keeps each source row as\n  the interaction datum.\n- `x: 'month'` and `y: 'revenue'` map existing source fields.\n- The unique month gives each observation stable positional identity across updates.\n- Compact scale factories infer domains from mark channels and own mapping behavior.\n- TanStack Charts copies those scales and assigns responsive pixel ranges.\n- `label`, `format`, and `grid` configure the axis guide without changing the scale.\n- Omitted margins are measured automatically from the rendered labels and titles.\n- `ariaLabel` names the chart; pointer and keyboard focus use the same inferred points.\n\nRead [Grammar of Graphics](./concepts/grammar-of-graphics.md) for the full model, then browse the [Example Gallery](./examples/index.md) for complete compositions.\n"}
